PASS Real source selections, edits/undo/redo and Reading mode count frontmatter only when selected, use reference numeric/punctuation/CJK/kana/Korean/Tamil/Tibetan rules and UTF-16 emoji/CRLF lengths without writing the note.
PASS Outline uses actual ATX/Setext metadata, excludes YAML/comments/indented and nested-length fences, nests skipped levels correctly, folds by pointer/keyboard/all controls and follows real source-cursor navigation.
PASS Dirty heading edits, undo/redo and external saved replacements refresh the real Outline; Reading heading navigation/scroll changes active highlighting and emits the actual public Markdown scroll event.
PASS Disable/re-enable removes owned Outline controls and retained listeners, restores counts, and full native restart or real-folder WASM reconnect retains the real files/mode without rewriting original workspace/community configuration.
PASS The real status control hides for empty/image leaves, honors explicit app.json Live Preview, offers checked keyboard/pointer Source/Reading/Live Preview choices and applies actual in-place Markdown styles without changing native getMode semantics or file bytes.
PASS Real formatted-text typing and task-checkbox input preserve selections, undo/redo, dirty buffers and community editor extensions across all three modes; only explicit save writes the exact original BOM/CRLF with the intended task marker changed.
PASS CodeMirror displays an actually decoded local image, rendered table and local Mermaid image; their real Edit buttons reveal original source and revoke resources, detached task controls are inert, and Ctrl-clicking a wiki alias opens the resolved heading in a separate real Reading leaf.
PASS Real split panes retain independent per-leaf modes with a shared document and community extensions; public same-file setViewState preserves unsaved text/history, rejects malformed source flags without disturbing the view, and retains opaque state.
PASS Actual external writes refresh clean Source/Live Preview peers, but conflicting saved bytes cannot overwrite a dirty shared buffer; the guarded save rejects visibly to its caller and explicit discard/reload retains the external BOM/CRLF document.
PASS Disabling Editor status removes its open menu, status button and retained listeners without disabling editing modes; native restart or actual-folder WASM reconnect preserves source flags, opaque leaf state and persisted plugin ownership while leaving app/workspace bytes and other enabled IDs unchanged.
PASS Actual selection extraction saves previously dirty text, creates a real nested target, resolves source/template links independently, carries image/reference/footnote definitions, and retains BOM/CRLF plus real source undo/redo.
PASS Cancel and retained closed-dialog controls write nothing; retargeted source views, unresolved relative-link transfers, post-open external/local edits and missing templates reject visibly without losing bytes, creating a target or implicitly saving concurrent local text.
PASS Heading extraction includes children and blocks, rejects duplicate target anchors, supports Shift+Enter prepend and embed/none replacements, and selectively repairs real Markdown/properties/Canvas while whole-note and remaining-section links stay on the source.
PASS Merge confirmation is enforced; a real preflight veto and a target changed after planning retain all source/reference files, newer target bytes and restored source panes.
PASS Confirmed merge combines precise YAML/body data with guarded source trash and Markdown/Canvas reference repair, opens its real target and emits one owned modification/deletion; a real file-menu action also merges a non-active note and Ctrl+Enter creates its new nested target.
PASS A real modify-event subscriber can edit an open target after commit: Note composer reports the committed-but-unsaved state, retains its text, disables repeat application and permits a normal subsequent save.
PASS Real select/template/confirmation settings preserve unknown BOM-prefixed configuration, disable removes owned commands/dialog/listeners, and desktop restart or real-folder browser reconnect restores both composed files and enabled runtime.
PASS An actual CommonJS plugin uses shared Menu/Item/Separator types, rich labels, checked/disabled rows, sections, viewport placement, pointer/keyboard actions and dismissal; real file/editor events carry the current TFile, MarkdownView and CodeMirror editor.
PASS Actual editor context actions retain copy/cut/select-all, undoable CRLF-aware paste, empty-paste preservation and visible permission/stale/multiple-selection errors using a bounded clipboard API fixture; the system clipboard is never read or changed.
PASS Closing the actual source view or disabling the plugin removes owned menus and retained button listeners; re-enable has exactly one event subscriber, and only explicit plugin toggles change community enablement.
PASS The actual opt-in converter previews Roam/Bear/tasks/numeric links and legacy frontmatter in real vault files; Cancel and a retained closed-dialog button write no notes.
PASS Confirmed legacy conversion rewrites the actual BOM/CRLF note with lossless unknown numeric/YAML data and refreshes its real clean editor; version-guarded Undo restores every original Markdown file byte-for-byte.
PASS Newer external versions, ambiguous numeric destinations and post-preview dirty edits reject visibly without partial note writes, implicit saves or loss of local text; generated link text disambiguates real files.
PASS Readable numeric aliases are a separate working conversion; disable removes real converter UI/ribbon/commands/listeners, and restart/reconnect restores enablement without altering unknown settings or original note bytes.
PASS Outgoing links lists real wiki/Markdown/property links and embeds, deduplicates the same destination/subpath, and explicitly disables unsupported attachment/traversal actions.
PASS Outgoing links navigates to exact heading/block context, creates a missing Markdown target without changing its source, and keeps a pinned sidebar on its note.
PASS Dirty-buffer edits, undo/redo, external saves and target renames refresh outgoing resolution without overwriting vault files or secretly rewriting links.
PASS Unlinked aliases navigate to their source; collapse/follow/pin state survives an actual reload and releasing the pin follows the active note.
PASS Disabling Outgoing links removes its commands, view and enabled-instance lookup; re-enabling creates one fresh view with the persisted state.
PASS Image Fit stays inside real fractional CSS viewports without feedback scrollbars, including width- and height-constrained images.
PASS Outgoing opens real decoded raster/Canvas leaves, honors modified-click tabs, follows provider registration/removal and preserves exact attachment bytes; image fit/zoom/scroll work and closed views release URLs and retained controls.
PASS Reading links share registered attachment navigation; live external pixel changes, visible decode errors/recovery and guarded image rename refresh the actual view without writing image bytes or losing opaque state.
PASS Actual image leaves, zoom, opaque state and pinned Outgoing restore after full desktop restart/browser reconnect while original workspace absence/bytes, Markdown and exact binary attachments stay preserved.
PASS Search executes real worker-backed Boolean/regex/path/file/tag/property/case queries and selects exact source context.
PASS Search waits for actual worker readiness, including a startup longer than two seconds, without charging it against the separate bounded query deadline.
PASS Search follows dirty edits/undo/redo, real external writes and renames, rejects invalid queries without stale results, and terminates a blocking regex off the UI thread.
PASS Tags lists nested inline/property tags with counts, excludes escaped/code/comment text, filters/folds/sorts, and uses the actual Search dependency with a visible disabled-dependency error.
PASS Backlinks resolves heading/block references and unlinked aliases, navigates exact source ranges, follows unsaved/undo/external/rename changes, and renders/removes real in-document backlinks.
PASS Footnotes shows multiline definitions, repeated references and explicit missing definitions, selects exact source ranges and updates through dirty edits/undo/redo.
PASS Search/Tags/Backlinks/Footnotes preserve real query/sort/fold/pin state across reload/reconnect; disabling removes owned views/controllers/commands and re-enabling creates one fresh instance.
PASS Quick switcher settings control actual registered attachments and unresolved references: Canvas opens, hidden attachments/unknown extensions stay out, and existing-only removes unresolved suggestions without implicitly creating a note.
PASS The unsupported-file toggle follows app.json, all-types overrides attachment filtering, URI-relative targets and explicit creation use real controls, and Boolean/opaque settings plus BOM survive reload/reconnect without rewriting app.json.
PASS Bookmarks opens actual heading/block, empty-folder and saved-search targets; distant Reading blocks scroll precisely and missing/unsupported targets reject without discarding data.
PASS Actual Bookmarks controls add groups/files, rename, reorder, move into groups, remove and filter; BOM, unknown data and note bytes survive, and obsolete controls cannot mutate newer data.
PASS The async core lifecycle honors an actual Bookmarks preflight veto without unloading its original view, removes owned controls/providers on disable, restores unavailable panes with their filters, and rejects concurrent reloads.
PASS Organized Bookmarks data and actual per-pane filter state survive a fresh runtime without modifying original note bytes.
PASS The actual Workspaces manager saves and loads real split/tab/pin/Reading/sidebar and core-view state, without hidden editors or rewriting original Obsidian profiles.
PASS Saved-layout preflight and staged view loading retain the actual previous editor/DOM on factory failures, explicit preflight vetoes and dirty-save conflicts; external note bytes are not overwritten.
PASS Named layouts can be renamed and deleted without deleting notes; guarded profiles, unknown configuration, UTF-8 BOM and the active layout survive a fresh runtime.
PASS Actual local Properties controls edit source/Reading notes, typed numbers, checkboxes and lists; body selections and existing undo/redo survive while exact numeric literals, comments, anchors, unknown structured/type data and BOM/CRLF are retained.
PASS Properties rejects unsafe numeric input, obsolete dialogs and dirty external-save conflicts without overwriting newer file bytes or discarding the original unsaved buffer.
PASS The real vault property catalog filters/sorts/counts, assigns case-insensitive types and renames a property in both notes and types.json; all-note collision preflight, unknown types/configuration and precise YAML/body bytes are preserved.
PASS Actual Properties owned views, filters, sort, pinned file and assigned types survive disable/re-enable and a fresh runtime; unsupported providers retain their saved states without hidden editors or note rewrites.
PASS The actual file explorer and native-shaped root actions create nested empty folders, retain root identity and reject occupied paths without replacing them or prefilling an absolute root.
PASS Real rename cancellation and destination collisions retain source/reference bytes, file identity and public event state.
PASS Pending file mutations cannot be dismissed with Escape or the dialog close button; a later failure stays visible and retains the source bytes.
PASS Rename/move preserves the actual TFile, shared sessions, Reading mode, pinned discovery/Properties panes and history while saving dirty text and rewriting real wiki/Markdown/reference/property links without changing exact YAML numbers or CRLF/BOM.
PASS Bookmarking an unmarked paragraph generates and saves a real block ID; a Windows case-only rename updates physical filenames and persists both heading and generated-block targets.
PASS Disabled attachment previews still expose real tree actions: binary move retains every byte and updates references; cancelled trash changes nothing and committed vault trash preserves a colliding folder.
PASS Trash saves dirty shared notes, honors a later pane's explicit preflight veto before disposing any editor, preserves undo/redo after rejection, and closes all associated sessions only when the note is actually trashed.
PASS Renamed files, split sessions, pinned properties and updated bookmarks reopen after a fresh runtime without changing original workspace.json; missing targets still reject explicitly.
PASS Global Graph uses actual Markdown/property links, missing and orphan notes; node clicks open/create real files and dirty edits, undo and external changes update the rendered graph.
PASS Local Graph has real directed depth and neighbor-edge controls, follows files unless pinned, and global/local nodes and file state follow an actual guarded rename.
PASS Actual Graph controls filter nodes, show attachments/tags, navigate to Search, reorder overlapping color groups and change visible sizes/arrows/physics while preserving BOM and unknown configuration fields.
PASS The real SVG graph supports camera zoom/pan, pointer node dragging and keyboard node activation without using a hidden editor.
PASS Malformed and excessive Graph queries fail visibly off the UI thread; stale configuration writes retain external bytes and Reload controls permits guarded subsequent saves.
PASS Graph disable/re-enable removes and restores owned commands/ribbon/views; global controls, local depth/pin/file and both cameras survive a full restart or folder-handle reconnect without rewriting the original Obsidian workspace.
PASS Existing Canvas text/file/web/group/unknown cards and edges open through the file explorer, render real Markdown/images and live dirty/undo/external file previews, and navigate actual headings without modifying original BOM/CRLF data or implicitly loading websites.
PASS Actual Canvas inspector typing autosaves the original versioned UTF-8 file; keyboard undo/redo works across saves while preserving BOM, CRLF and unknown JSON fields.
PASS Real Canvas pointer/keyboard input selects and grid-snaps cards, resizes, connects by toolbar and handle drag, edits edge labels, moves groups with contained cards, rejects invalid geometry and retains deletion undo.
PASS Stale Canvas autosaves retain external disk bytes and the dirty board; actual native reload confirmations honor cancellation and explicit discard before installing a clean document.
PASS Guarded note and binary renames update stored Canvas file cards, real text-card Markdown and group backgrounds together, retaining unknown card data and every attachment byte.
PASS Canvas commands create collision-safe files in the configured folder; actual wheel/modifier/Shift, label and snapping settings apply while BOM and future configuration survive.
PASS Actual Canvas selects and slider cover folder/current/root placement, retained conditional folder values, detail thresholds at both bounds and Restore default without modifying the existing board.
PASS All six modifier-drag preferences run through real rectangle input, including reverse geometry, shared menu, note/media selection, safe website errors, cancel/detached controls and saved undo without writing referenced files.
PASS Canvas disable/re-enable and a fresh runtime restore its actual file, camera DOM transform, settings and unknown JSON without hidden editors, leaked providers or original workspace rewrites.
